<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Teanum Sidicinum</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Teano</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Teanum Sidicinum, modern Teano in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/campania">Campania</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, was the chief town of the Oscan-speaking Sidicini, set in the hills between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roccamonfina">Roccamonfina</a> volcano and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volturno">Volturno</a>. Their conflict with the Samnites in 343 BCE drew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> into its first war with Samnium. It later became a Roman town on the Via Latina, whose <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theatre">theatre</a> and other remains survive.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/teanum-sidicinum.jpg" alt="Teanum Sidicinum" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Specializedturin at Italian Wikipedia · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Teanopanorama.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
